---
/* LA COMPARATIVA, EN UN SOLO SITIO.

   Vivia dentro de results/index.astro y ademas hubo una copia en la home. Las
   dos divergieron: distinta cuarta fila, y a la de Results le faltaban los
   `data-label`, que son los que en movil ponen el nombre de la columna encima de
   cada dato. Sin ellos cada celda pintaba una etiqueta VACIA.

   Ahora se declara aqui y la montan las dos paginas. Cual de las dos depende de
   SHOW_RESULTS: encendido va en Results, apagado se muda a la home. Nunca las
   dos a la vez.

   EL ORDEN DE LAS FILAS NO ES LIBRE. "Risk to the release" es la unica celda de
   toda la tabla donde admitimos algo en vez de ganar, y va la CUARTA. El pie
   dice que la ultima fila es el argumento entero, y ese argumento es publicar el
   metodo, no reconocer un riesgo. Al final, la tabla cerraria admitiendo algo
   justo antes del boton. */
import { url } from '../lib/site';

interface Props { intro?: boolean }
const { intro = true } = Astro.props;

const COLS = ['Paid playlist placements', 'Agency retainer', 'Running ads yourself'] as const;

const ROWS = [
  { label: 'What you get',
    cells: ['Streams from accounts that never come back', 'A deck, monthly', 'Reach, if the targeting is right'],
    us: 'Listeners who save and follow' },
  { label: 'What it costs',
    cells: ['Per placement, with no floor', 'Monthly retainer, three-month minimum', 'Ad spend plus your own week'],
    us: 'Ad spend plus one flat fee' },
  { label: 'Who keeps the pixel',
    cells: ['Not applicable', 'Usually the agency', 'You'],
    us: 'You, always' },
  { label: 'Risk to the release',
    cells: ['Bot flags and playlist removal', 'Slow to react mid-campaign', 'Budget burnt learning'],
    us: 'Ad spend that does not convert. Nothing you are locked into' },
  { label: 'Can you check the method',
    cells: ['No', 'No', 'Only your own'],
    us: 'Yes. We publish it before you pay' },
];
---
{intro && (
  <p class="sec-intro">
    Four ways to spend money on a release, compared on five things. Three of the four
    we would talk you out of. One row admits what can go wrong here, and the last row
    is the one only we can write.
  </p>
)}

<div class="cmp-scroll" data-rvl>
  <table class="cmp">
    <thead>
      <tr>
        <th class="cmp-lab"><span class="visually-hidden">Comparison</span></th>
        {COLS.map((c) => <th>{c}</th>)}
        <th class="cmp-us">109MUSIC</th>
      </tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
      {ROWS.map((r) => (
        <tr>
          <th class="cmp-lab" scope="row">{r.label}</th>
          {r.cells.map((cell, i) => <td data-label={COLS[i]}>{cell}</td>)}
          <td data-label="109MUSIC" class="cmp-us">{r.us}</td>
        </tr>
      ))}
    </tbody>
  </table>
</div>
<p class="cmp-foot mono">
  The last row is the whole argument. Everything under{' '}
  <a href={url('/music-marketing/')}>Music Marketing</a> is what we run for clients,
  written down.
</p>
